#: ../../../reference/interfaces/kernel-module-load-interface.md:0
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/kernel-module-load-interface.md:8
msgid "kernel-module-load interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/kernel-module-load-interface.md:10
msgid ""
"`kernel-module-load` provides the ability to load, or deny loading, specific "
"kernel modules. This interface gives privileged access to the device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/kernel-module-load-interface.md:12
msgid ""
"See also the {ref}`kernel-module-control interface <interfaces-kernel-module-"
"control-interface>` for inserting, removing and querying kernel modules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/kernel-module-load-interface.md:15
msgid "Developer details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/kernel-module-load-interface.md:17
msgid ""
"**{ref}`Auto-connect <explanation-interfaces-interface-auto-connection>`**: "
"no<br /> **{ref}`Super-privileged <reference-operations-interfaces-super-"
"privileged-interfaces>`**: yes</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/kernel-module-load-interface.md:17
msgid "<br />"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/kernel-module-load-interface.md:17
msgid "</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/kernel-module-load-interface.md:21
msgid ""
"This interface controls a resource shared by the whole system. Snaps that "
"use it can be installed as parallel instances, but every instance acts on "
"the same system resource and snapd does not coordinate between them. Make "
"sure each instance manages different resources, or run only one instance at "
"a time. See {ref}`Snaps that are unsupported as parallel instances "
"<interfaces-parallel-installs-shared-resources>` for details.."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/kernel-module-load-interface.md:24
msgid "**Attributes**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/kernel-module-load-interface.md:25
msgid ""
"`name` (plug, required): provides the name of the kernel module to be loaded "
"(eg, '`name: pcspkr`')"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/kernel-module-load-interface.md:26
msgid ""
"`load` (plug): string to declare when, or whether, to load this module. "
"Values can be one of the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/kernel-module-load-interface.md:27
msgid ""
"`on-boot` (default): loads the kernel module at boot time (eg. `load: on-"
"boot`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/kernel-module-load-interface.md:28
msgid ""
"`denied`: prevents the module from being loaded at all (eg. `load: denied`). "
"Also known as _denylisting_ in the Linux kernel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/kernel-module-load-interface.md:29
msgid ""
"`dynamic`: enables runtime loading and unloading of the kernel module. The "
"snap can load and unload the module using snapctl kmod."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/kernel-module-load-interface.md:30
msgid ""
"`options` (plug): string of options to use when loading the module (eg, "
"`options: p1=3 p2=true p3`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/kernel-module-load-interface.md:32
msgid ""
"**In addition to the `name` attribute being required, either `options` or "
"`load` must also be specified.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/kernel-module-load-interface.md:34
msgid ""
"Consumers of this interface require a {ref}`snap declaration <interfaces-"
"process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks>` for distribution via the "
"Snap Store."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/kernel-module-load-interface.md:36
msgid "Requires snapd version _2.54+_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/kernel-module-load-interface.md:38
msgid "<h3 id='heading-code'>Code examples</h3>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/kernel-module-load-interface.md:40
msgid ""
"The following is an example snippet for an application snap to load the "
"module `foo` with options `param=2`, and to deny loading the module `bar`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/kernel-module-load-interface.md:42
msgid ""
"plugs:\n"
"  load-foo:\n"
"    interface: kernel-module-load\n"
"    modules:\n"
"    - name: foo\n"
"      options: param=2\n"
"  deny-bar:\n"
"    interface: kernel-module-load\n"
"    modules:\n"
"    - name: bar\n"
"      load: denied\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/kernel-module-load-interface.md:56
msgid ""
"The `load-foo` _foo_ kernel module can be more verbosely by declared with "
"the `load` attribute, resulting in the same behaviour:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/kernel-module-load-interface.md:58
msgid ""
"plugs:\n"
"  load-foo:\n"
"    interface: kernel-module-load\n"
"    modules:\n"
"    - name: foo\n"
"      load: on-boot\n"
"      options: param=2\n"
msgstr ""

